system/network capabilities when explicitly required, and opaque authority material.

## PM-ARCH-004 — External Origin Isolation

External URLs/help/docs/Provider pages open in a separate unprivileged context without the Manager bridge.

## PM-ARCH-005 — Devtools Boundary

Production remote debugging/devtools remain disabled unless explicitly governed by Developer/Test authority.

## PM-ARCH-006 — Broker Failure

Broker failure immediately removes privileged UI capability. Renderer enters unprivileged disconnected mode and purges protected broker-origin state as required.

## PM-ARCH-007 — Client Instance Continuity

Broker/process restart does not automatically preserve Manager client identity. Continuity requires mechanical proof from Prime application/session authority; otherwise a new client instance is minted.

## PM-MANAGER-POLICY-001 — Renderer/Broker Profiles

Renderer and broker use separate scoped Profiles/Policies or mechanically equivalent isolation. Manager is not made UID 0 simply to survive pressure or access Core.

## PM-MANAGER-POLICY-002 — No Unproven SYSTEM_UTILITY Escape Hatch

A new broad privileged system class is not invented merely to make Manager harder to kill. Any such class requires separate Prime architecture review/proof.

## PM-DISTRESS-001 — Manager Distress Properties

PM0 freezes the dimensions and provisional ceilings for:

- renderer/broker memory;
- relative OOM posture;
- CPU scheduling posture;
- I/O posture;
- control responsiveness;
- telemetry/detail shedding;
- renderer restartability;
- minimum distress function set.

Actual production envelope is measured in PM1/PM1.5.

