# F. CURRENT CORE AUTHORITY

## PM-CORE-001 — Core Authority Lease

Only one active Core mutation authority exists per Host authority domain. Epoch alone is not exclusivity.

## PM-CORE-002 — Enforced Exclusivity

Supervisor/kernel/privilege infrastructure or equivalent independently enforces the Core Authority Lease/fence.

## PM-CORE-003 — Core Lease Lifecycle

Core Authority Lease defines acquisition, active ownership, fencing/revocation, loss/recovery, and terminal release. Successor authority is not granted merely because a timeout fired; the prior authority must be fenced or reconciled.

## PM-CORE-004 — Stale Core Revocation

A superseded Core loses authority to admit mutations, issue Provider commands, create current AuthorizationDecisions, publish authoritative current projections, or append new Core-authoritative evidence/audit.

## PM-CORE-005 — Privileged Handle Fencing

Old Core cannot retain reusable privileged Host mutation handles after losing the lease.

## PM-CORE-006 — Core IPC Authentication

Broker authenticates the current Core authority identity/epoch, not merely a socket pathname or UID.

