# G. AUTH, SESSION, TIME, AND ASSURANCE

## PM-AUTHN-001 — Principal Identity

Principal identity is opaque/incarnation-safe. Username/display name is presentation only. Deleted/recreated names do not inherit prior authority/history.

## PM-AUTHN-002 — Login Session Lifecycle

Portable states include `ESTABLISHING`, `ACTIVE_UNLOCKED`, `LOCKED`, and `TERMINATED`, with explicit user-switch/issuer-restart semantics.

## PM-AUTHN-003 — Session Invalidation Effects

Lock/logout/user-switch/issuer/security-state changes define effects on disclosure contexts, approval challenges, assurance claims, candidate requests, and subscriptions. Unlock never resurrects expired elevation.

## PM-AUTHN-004 — Credential Boundary

Manager never receives passwords, PINs, biometric material, passkeys, or reusable credentials.

## PM-TIME-001 — Security Time Basis

Wall clock is not the sole authority for grants, preflights, executor leases, support validity, or other security expiry. Security-sensitive time uses issuer-owned monotonic/lease/secure-time semantics with conservative invalidation when continuity is uncertain.

## PM-ASSUR-001 — Typed Assurance Claims

Examples include `AUTHENTICATED_SESSION`, `RECENT_REAUTH`, `TRUSTED_LOCAL_USER_PRESENCE`, `TRUSTED_REMOTE_HUMAN_APPROVAL`, `AUTHORIZED_AUTOMATION`, and `RECOVERY_AUTHORITY`.

## PM-ASSUR-002 — Assurance Predicate

Effect descriptors define typed assurance predicates over claim type, issuer/epoch, Host, principal, session, audience, interaction Provider, freshness, presence semantics, and explicit conjunction/disjunction.

## PM-ASSUR-003 — Incomparability

No generic scalar ranking substitutes unrelated claim types. Unknown/incomparable claims fail closed.

## PM-ASSUR-004 — Trusted Local Approval Mechanism

Trusted approval requires a compositor/system-owned reserved security presentation plus trusted input provenance that ordinary renderer z-order/input injection cannot satisfy.

## PM-ASSUR-005 — High-Risk Consent Disclosure

If Prime cannot legally disclose enough Core-resolved target/effect information for the operator to distinguish what is being approved, that human-confirmed high-risk operation is unavailable.

## PM-ASSUR-006 — Approval Challenge Lifecycle

Trusted approval challenges define `ISSUED`, `APPROVED`, `DENIED`, `EXPIRED`, `CANCELLED`, and `INVALIDATED` or equivalent. Terminal state never reopens. Session/issuer/preflight changes invalidate affected challenges. Rate/concurrency bounds prevent prompt flooding.

